Chapter 7 — The Selector as a Learning Problem

7.1 Hypothesis classes

Let \mathcal{H} be a class of selectors \varphi:\Sigma^n\to\{0,\dots,k\}. We consider:

· \mathcal{H}_{\mathrm{fix}}: constants \varphi\equiv i.
· \mathcal{H}_{\mathrm{thr}}: threshold rules on a scalar feature (e.g., zero‑order entropy).
· \mathcal{H}_{\mathrm{tree},d}: decision trees of depth \le d.
· \mathcal{H}_{\mathrm{lin}}: linear thresholds over m features.

The VC dimension of a depth‑d tree with L=2^d leaves is \Theta(L\log L). Uniform convergence bounds based on VC dimension are vacuous at m\sim10^3–10^4 when L is in the hundreds.

7.2 Theorem 7.1 (McAllester PAC‑Bayes regret bound)

Let P be a prior over \mathcal{H}, Q a posterior, and

\ell(\varphi,x)=L_\varphi(x)-L_A(x)\in[0,n]

under identical framing and admissible actions. For m i.i.d. samples and any \delta\in(0,1), with probability at least 1-\delta over the sample,

\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\mathbb{E}_{\varphi\sim Q}[\ell(\varphi,x)]
\;\le\;
\frac{1}{m}\sum_{j=1}^m\mathbb{E}_{\varphi\sim Q}[\ell(\varphi,x^{(j)})]
\;+\;
n\sqrt{\frac{\mathrm{KL}(Q\|P)+\log\!\bigl(\frac{2m}{\delta}\bigr)}{2m}}.

Proof. McAllester's PAC‑Bayes bound for bounded losses; see the standard form with m samples and confidence \delta. The loss interval is [0,n] because L_A is the candidate‑set minimum under the same contract and L_\varphi\ge L_A by Theorem 5.2. \square

7.3 Corollary 7.2 (Vacuity test)

Compute the right‑hand side of Theorem 7.1 numerically at the thesis's actual m, n, and \mathrm{KL}(Q\|P). If it exceeds n (the trivial bound on [0,n]), declare the bound vacuous and report cross‑validated regret with bootstrap confidence intervals instead.

PAC‑Bayes bounds are often numerically vacuous at small sample sizes; the framework's advantage is conditional on the KL term being small relative to the capacity term. A vacuous theorem is not a contribution.

7.4 Temporal dependence

Randomly splitting adjacent packets from the same telemetry stream can produce optimistically biased held‑out estimates. The protocol should split by time block or mission segment, not by individual packet, and should report the split unit alongside the regret estimate.

