I.15 Regret Geometry (Ch. 5, Theorem 5.2)

```
  For a fixed input x:

     L_A(x)  =  min( n , b+c+min_i s_i(x) )    ← floor
                          ▲
                          │
     L_B(x)  =  min( n , b+c+s_{φ(x)}(x) )     ← depends on φ

  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │                                                     │
  │  lengths:                                           │
  │                                                     │
  │     n ──────────────────────  RAW (always 200)      │
  │                                                     │
  │  b+c+s_{φ(x)} ──────────────  B's choice            │
  │                            ╲                        │
  │                             ╲  regret = L_B - L_A   │
  │                              ╲                      │
  │  b+c+min_i s_i ──────────────●  A's choice          │
  │                                                     │
  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Theorem 5.2:  L_B(x) ≥ L_A(x) for all x.
  Equality  ⟺  φ(x) attains the candidate-set minimum.
  Regret    =  L_B(x) - L_A(x)  ∈ [0, n].
```

